<%#
  "Poslali smo ti poruku" — the waiting room of the one-step registration, for
  a citizen who is NOT signed in yet. The body is the same one delivery A's
  phone-verification page renders; all this page owns is where its own actions
  live, its own copy scope, the hand-off sentence and the field that takes a
  corrected number.

  Three differences from A's page, all deliberate:
  * the status poll is a POST (R-D4) — it can sign this browser in, and that
    must never be something a GET does;
  * "wrong number" does not send the citizen back to a phone form they have no
    session for; the number is re-entered here (see the controller's #change);
  * that number field is shown only to the browser that did the registering.
    Pointing the verification at a different phone decides who ends up owning
    the account, and the mailed reminder is a credential that reached an
    address nobody has proven. Whoever holds only that link gets the honest
    alternative instead: start over, which destroys the never-verified account
    rather than redirecting it.

  The copy scope carries pending.reverify_lead even though this page can never
  enter reverify mode (Registration::PendingAccess refuses a granted account,
  so @reverify is never set here): the shared body reads that one key while
  building the page whatever mode it is in. The rest of the reverify copy is
  delivery A's alone and is deliberately not duplicated here.
%>
<% add_decidim_page_title(t(".title")) %>

<main class="wrapper">
  <div class="mi-surface">
    <% if @change_number %>
      <section class="mi-account-panel" data-mi-new-phone>
        <h2><%= t(".new_phone_title") %></h2>
        <p><%= t(".new_phone_hint") %></p>
        <%= form_with url: pending_action_path("/ponovo"), method: :post, class: "mi-account-settings-form" do %>
          <label for="mi-new-phone"><%= t(".new_phone_label") %></label>
          <input id="mi-new-phone" type="tel" name="phone" inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel" required>
          <button type="submit" class="mi-btn mi-btn--primary mi-btn--sm"><%= t(".new_phone_submit") %></button>
        <% end %>
      </section>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "decidim/bih/phone_verification/message_sent",
               scope: "decidim.bih.registrations.pending",
               masked_phone: masked_phone,
               expired: @expired,
               status_url: pending_action_path("/status"),
               status_method: "post",
               confirm_url: pending_action_path("/kod"),
               resend_url: (phone_on_record.present? ? pending_action_path("/ponovo") : nil),
               change_url: pending_page_path,
               check_url: pending_page_path %>

    <% if @handoff %>
      <p class="mi-phone-verification__handoff" data-mi-handoff><%= t(".handoff") %></p>
    <% else %>
      <section class="mi-account-panel" data-mi-start-over>
        <p><%= t(".start_over_hint") %></p>
        <%= button_to t(".start_over"), pending_action_path("/pocni-ispocetka"),
                      method: :post, class: "mi-btn mi-btn--ghost mi-btn--sm" %>
      </section>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</main>
